From aa0faae4538ca4dcd6143f82e3922ec69826543f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yin Li <kevinli.ai.work@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:38:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf][Beam Search] Rank beam candidates before building
 their histories

Each offline beam search step asks for 2 * beam_width logprobs per beam, so it
produces 2 * beam_width**2 candidates, and _beam_search_step built a full
BeamSearchSequence for every one of them - `tokens=current_beam.tokens +
[token_id]`, `logprobs=current_beam.logprobs + [logprobs]` - before sorting and
keeping beam_width. A beam's tokens start with the whole prompt
(BeamSearchInstance seeds them with prompt_token_ids), so every candidate
copied prompt + generated tokens, and almost all of those copies were thrown
away.

Rank first, build after: each candidate is scored from its parent's length
plus one, its last token and its cumulative logprob via a new
get_beam_search_score_from_length() (get_beam_search_score now delegates to
it, so both are the same arithmetic), candidates are sorted with the same
stable reverse sort, and only the survivors are materialized. EOS completions
are still built and appended to `completed` immediately, in the original
order. The engine calls, candidate count, scores and results are unchanged;
only the discarded histories are no longer built.

Measured on the real LLM.beam_search driven by a fake engine (CPU only, one
pinned core, median of 5 runs, beam-logic time per step with the fake
engine's own time subtracted):

  beam  prompt   main      this change
     4   4096    0.33 ms   0.08 ms
     8   1024    0.50 ms   0.11 ms
     8   4096    1.59 ms   0.17 ms
    16   4096   14.20 ms   0.47 ms
    32   1024   15.44 ms   1.25 ms
    32   4096   52.77 ms   1.54 ms
    64   1024   95.18 ms   6.05 ms

On main the cost grows with prompt length; with the change it barely does,
which is the copy being removed. This is CPU time between engine steps, on
the critical path of every step; how much of end-to-end step time it is
depends on the model and has not been measured here.

Equivalence: 640 full beam_search runs (beam width 1-8, EOS rate up to 0.4,
heavy logprob ties, ignore_eos, length_penalty 0/1/2) produce byte-identical
outputs on main and on this change - tokens, scores as exact float bit
patterns, every step's logprobs, finish reasons.

Tests: get_beam_search_score_from_length matches get_beam_search_score, and
_beam_search_step matches an eager build-then-sort reference including ties,
EOS and ignore_eos; an off-by-one length or a changed tie order fails it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
